    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Maths holds a bittersweet place for me—my dad studied engineering, but he never taught it at home. In school, I loved puzzles and problem-solving, but the rigid rules made some concepts feel like puzzle pieces that didn’t fit. Now, as an unemployed immigrant in Philadelphia, I use math daily for budgeting and planning my volunteering work with local youth programs.",
